*   Cost to plant: $90 (initial cost)
    *   Annual production: 7 lemons
    *   Price per lemon: $1.5
    *   Annual cost (watering/feeding): $3
    *   Goal: Find the number of years until he starts earning money (break-even).

    *   Annual revenue = 7 lemons * $1.5/lemon = $10.50
    *   Annual cost = $3.00
    *   Annual profit = Annual revenue - Annual cost = $10.50 - $3.00 = $7.50

    *   Total cost = $90
    *   Years needed = Total cost / Annual profit
    *   Years needed = $90 / $7.50

    *   90 / 7.5 = 900 / 75
    *   900 / 75 = 180 / 15 (Divide by 5)
    *   180 / 15 = 12

    *   After 11 years: 11 * $7.50 = $82.50 (Not enough)
    *   After 12 years: 12 * $7.50 = $90.00 (Break-even)
